FRRouting 10.6.1 (Alpine package frr-10.6.1-r0)
License: GPL-2.0-or-later (Alpine package metadata).
Upstream source: https://github.com/FRRouting/frr/tree/frr-10.6.1
Exact distribution recipe: https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports/-/tree/23a7c9f1a27473a1a8a09ad3433d4a7a5b0fb62c/community/frr
Official package URLs and SHA256 checksums are recorded in PROVENANCE.json.
The package is installed with Alpine signature verification. Packaging does not
start any routing daemon or enable BGP runtime capability. bgpd must use
--no_kernel with managed zebra observation; Tunnex owns learned kernel routes.

Managed zebra observer is built from the exact pinned upstream source archive
recorded in PROVENANCE.json. zebra-no-sys-admin.patch removes only initial
SYS_ADMIN demand and explicitly refuses namespace VRF backend; unused bfdd,
staticd and watchfrr are disabled. Its source-built libfrr is isolated through
/opt/tunnex-bgp/lib RPATH. Signed packaged bgpd/vtysh keep packaged libraries.
Bgpd uses supported -S within the container's existing capability bounding set
and -n (no kernel installs); no SYS_ADMIN capability is added to the node.
